    'The RMI combines the ultrasound score (U: 0, 1 or 3 based on multilocularity, solid areas, metastases, ascites, bilaterality), menopausal status (M: 1 premenopausal, 3 postmenopausal) and serum CA-125 (U × M × CA-125). An RMI above 200–250 indicates high risk of ovarian cancer and need for referral to a gynaecological oncology multidisciplinary team for staging (CT) and cytoreductive surgery with platinum-based chemotherapy. Here RMI = 3 × 3 × 650 = 5,850. Other models include IOTA rules and the ADNEX model.',
