    'A 6-month-old has clusters of sudden flexion of the trunk, neck and limbs on waking, with developmental regression. EEG shows chaotic high-voltage slow waves and multifocal spikes. What is the syndrome, and which treatment is first-line in tuberous sclerosis?',
